    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required accepting an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR) on the owner request and returning a derived `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given. Since the test writes via `POST /api/owners` and reads back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, the title had to persist end-to-end.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (enum MR/MRS/MS/DR) to the `OwnerFields` schema so it binds from the request body, and added a read-only `salutation` string to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` column (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, so the title survives to the `GET` read-back.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `salutation` mapping expression: `title` blank/null \u2192 `lastName`, otherwise `title + \" \" + lastName`. Title itself maps automatically by name (MapStruct handles the DTO-enum \u2194 entity-String conversion, and `.name()` matches the enum values), so it flows request \u2192 entity \u2192 response.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table in every dialect (tests run on hsqldb; the rest kept consistent).\n\nVerification: `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` (title `DR`, lastName `who` \u2192 `salutation` = `\"DR who\"`) passes, and the full `mvnw test` run reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures or errors.",
